# Repository line-ending policy.
#
# Every platform checks out text files with LF. Windows Git defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites *.sh to CRLF; the bash test runners then
# fail immediately with "set: pipefail: invalid option name" because the CR is
# parsed as part of the option word. Keeping the worktree LF (and normalising
# to LF in the object database) makes the documented WSL/Linux commands in
# spec/AGENT-操作指南.md reproducible from a Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf
